## Scripts and helpers (no redundant tools)

Isiac rule (2026-11-21): **Do not** add a script or helper when the app, repo, or platform already covers it. Search first (`rg` / codebase search). Each **new** `scripts/*.ps1` (or harness helper) in a PR must state in the PR body **why existing paths are insufficient**.

### Existing map (repo `main`)

| Path | Role |
|---|---|
| `scripts/Prepare-TestIdentity.ps1` | Rewrites manifest to a **test** Identity (never `C20A7629`) |
| `BuildAndRun.ps1` | Build/run under test identity only; refuses release Identity |
| `ui-tests.ps1` | Live UI Automation suite against a running PID; FenrirDesktop gate; Studio S7 |
| `scripts/StudioDpiHarness.ps1` | **Canonical** FENRIR-STUDIO DPI / client-DIP resize / XamlRoot gate / SendInput drag library — dot-source this; do not invent sibling capture harnesses |
| `scripts/wt-list-prune-safe.ps1` | List/prune clean **merged** Palace worktrees above cap (byte-identical with hub/core); dry-run default |
| `scripts/sync-appx-version.py` | Sync `Package.appxmanifest` Identity Version from `PalaceVersion` |
| `scripts/check-version.py` | CI version / identity gates |
| `scripts/check-ps1-ascii.py` | ASCII-only check for PowerShell (Windows PowerShell 5.1) |
| `scripts/gen-imaging-fixtures.py` | Imaging test fixtures |

### Fold discipline

- Future Fenrir/Studio captures **dot-source** `StudioDpiHarness.ps1` and keep only scenario shot loops elsewhere. Prefer extending StudioDpi over new harness files.
- Do **not** revive store media one-shots (`capture-196*`, `capture-197*`) as living owners.
- App behaviors for tests = real UI/app code only — never side scripts writing the catalog DB.
- `.ps1` files stay ASCII-only so Windows PowerShell 5.1 can parse them.
